Definitely 3.0j is highly recommended. There were bugs in the termcap
and curses library used to compile earlier versions, which may explain the
problems Holger was having. I'm pretty sure I tested 3.0j under MGR and
it worked; make sure that you have "nocolor" and "noIBM_BIOS" set in your
nethack.cnf file if you're running under MGR. (nocolor because MGR doesn't
do color, and noIBM_BIOS to tell NetHack not to use the BIOS for I/O;
IBM_BIOS is a misnomer, and will be renamed to just plain "BIOS" in 3.1).

> The reason that I'm posting instead of e-mailing is that I have an
> additional question:  does anyone know now to run in color under MiNT?
> I know the right escape sequences, but termcap doesn't seem to have a
> "set character color" attribute to put them in.  Ideas?

You run in color under MiNT the same way you do under TOS -- just make
sure "IBM_BIOS" is set in nethack.cnf, and launch the program. NetHack
will then change the screen colors and set up escape sequences
(based on the ST's built-in VT52) automatically. If this doesn't work
please let me know. (Running in color under MW or BGACC isn't possible,
if that's what you wanted to know, because neither of those programs
implement the ST's color escape codes in a fully compatible way.)
